        "id": 6173,
        "name": "cajunjoel",
        "username": "cajunjoel1",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/c/d6d6ee/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2012-08-19T02:38:09.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>So with this new forum, we have this thing called \"Text Format\" below the body field when posting a topic or reply to a forum.</p><p>The text format is used to either allow you to use BBCode or a WYSIWYG editor. Until tonight, these were separate items. With the addition of the \"Quote\" button (w00t!) we've added functionality that merges the two together.</p><p>So you can either use the toolbar icons, which will show you what your post looks like as you type it.</p><p><strong>&nbsp; &nbsp;OR</strong></p><p>You can use BBCode&nbsp;<em>without selecting BBCode in the Text Format.&nbsp;&nbsp;</em>Given this, you may never need to use the BBCode text format again.&nbsp;</p><p>The system doesn't much care which version you use, but both will work and you can even mix them.&nbsp;(The reason for this is because the quote button will use BBCode to place the quote into a \"Filtered HTML\" box. Go figure.)</p><p><span>As always, you can use the quote icon in the toolbar to quote some text, but it won't automatically include another person's name. :)</span></p><p>So have at it. We may continue to tweak how the quotes appear as time goes on, but that's a definite bonus.</p><p>--Joel</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:36:02.248Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
