      {
        "id": 36411,
        "name": "Rabit",
        "username": "Rabit",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/rabit/{size}/7330_2.png",
        "created_at": "2012-08-23T15:40:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"cajunjoel\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/cajunjoel/48/1846_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> cajunjoel:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>So have at it. We may continue to tweak how the quotes appear as time goes on, but that's a definite bonus.–Joel</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Thought I'd give this a try to see how it worked. I'm <em>especially</em> interested in how the use of BBCode within the <span class=\"bbcode-i\">formatted</span> text will work. I'd tried a post earlier with the <strong>URL</strong> <span class=\"bbcode-b\">BBCode</span> tag that failed, so I'm going to give it a try, here.</p>\n<p><a href=\"http://sentinelsofthemultiverse.com/\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">Here's a normal link</a> and <a href=\"http://sentinelsofthemultiverse.com/\" data-bbcode=\"true\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">here's a BBCode link</a>.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong>Results</strong>:&nbsp;It ignored the bold (\"[<span class=\"bbcode-b\">b]\" /&nbsp;\"[</span>/b]\")&nbsp;and italicized (\"[<span class=\"bbcode-i\">i]\" / \"[</span>/i]\") BBCodes and displays the url codes without processing (which is what I experienced in my earlier post).</p>",
